1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:01,720
[Disclaimer: Characters, locations,
and all depicted events are fictional

2
00:00:01,740 --> 00:00:03,470
and for entertainment purposes only;
viewer discretion is advised]

3
00:00:12,180 --> 00:00:17,460
[Your Third Series]

4
00:00:17,790 --> 00:00:19,670
But this man loves you very much.

5
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:24,620
I think

6
00:00:24,760 --> 00:00:26,280
you should just say yes.

7
00:00:26,710 --> 00:00:28,700
Thinking about it
already gives me a headache.

8
00:00:29,710 --> 00:00:30,770
It was me

9
00:00:33,190 --> 00:00:35,200
who sent those men to get rid of Sarm

10
00:00:35,890 --> 00:00:36,400
Oh.

11
00:00:43,150 --> 00:00:44,170
What the fuck is this shit, huh?!

12
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:48,430
Jam!

13
00:00:48,430 --> 00:00:48,820
Jam.

14
00:00:49,330 --> 00:00:50,190
That bastard did this to you?

15
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:01,630
Stop it, Thee!

16
00:01:01,630 --> 00:01:03,720
If you hurt Mr. Sarm in any way,

17
00:01:03,740 --> 00:01:04,670
I will shoot!

18
00:01:37,910 --> 00:01:38,800
How are you?

19
00:01:39,890 --> 00:01:40,900
Are you hurt?

20
00:01:43,610 --> 00:01:46,009
Why should you care at all, Uncle?

21
00:01:48,430 --> 00:01:51,180
I was the one
who sent the men to get rid of your son.

22
00:01:54,720 --> 00:01:56,280
Because I know that

23
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:00,120
at your core...

24
00:02:00,900 --> 00:02:02,180
you're not a bad guy.

25
00:02:08,490 --> 00:02:09,259
I...

26
00:02:10,940 --> 00:02:12,200
I'm truly sorry.

27
00:02:17,230 --> 00:02:19,050
I want to own Adisuan Farm.

28
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:22,450
I've been wanting
to own it for years now.

29
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:25,610
Half a year ago,

30
00:02:26,850 --> 00:02:28,350
Sarm disappeared.

31
00:02:29,770 --> 00:02:31,370
Everyone knew that he was heartbroken

32
00:02:31,370 --> 00:02:33,140
and wouldn't return soon.

33
00:02:33,520 --> 00:02:35,400
So I used that opportunity

34
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:40,140
to send men to hunt him down

35
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:42,860
so that he'd be gone for good.

36
00:02:43,100 --> 00:02:45,060
Then, people would assume that

37
00:02:46,410 --> 00:02:47,720
Sarm was so hurt

38
00:02:48,670 --> 00:02:50,260
that he wanted to live
by the sea forever

39
00:02:52,600 --> 00:02:54,350
and had gone missing.

40
00:02:55,820 --> 00:02:57,200
Once the plan came to fruition,

41
00:02:57,840 --> 00:02:59,650
Adisuan Farm would probably belong to me.

42
00:02:59,980 --> 00:03:02,750
No one is better suited
to run Adisuan Farm than me.

43
00:03:03,250 --> 00:03:04,630
You also knew that

44
00:03:06,160 --> 00:03:07,550
when Sarm was still away,

45
00:03:07,570 --> 00:03:08,900
I embezzled money,

46
00:03:09,320 --> 00:03:10,700
falsified accounting records,

47
00:03:11,730 --> 00:03:13,170
and forged documents.

48
00:03:14,300 --> 00:03:16,920
I was trying to take over
Adisuan Farm bit by bit,

49
00:03:24,060 --> 00:03:25,550
then Sarm came back.

50
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:29,390
And weren't you aware that

51
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:32,140
Sarm also knew?

52
00:03:35,490 --> 00:03:36,910
I found it strange myself.

53
00:03:41,900 --> 00:03:44,200
Why did he choose to leave me be
despite knowing everything?

54
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:49,070
Because my son

55
00:03:50,500 --> 00:03:52,480
valued the bond you two shared.

56
00:03:54,590 --> 00:03:56,030
Do you despise me, Uncle?

57
00:04:08,980 --> 00:04:10,500
Do I?

58
00:04:16,529 --> 00:04:17,720
I don't, actually.

59
00:04:21,470 --> 00:04:22,900
Whether or not...

60
00:04:26,310 --> 00:04:27,740
I'd forgive you, though?

61
00:04:31,080 --> 00:04:32,100
It's still too soon.

62
00:04:37,430 --> 00:04:39,070
Do you know what the consequences

63
00:04:39,080 --> 00:04:40,420
of your action are?

64
00:04:45,080 --> 00:04:47,010
Let this

65
00:04:48,610 --> 00:04:49,770
be a lesson to you.

66
00:04:56,010 --> 00:04:57,440
Every day

67
00:04:59,070 --> 00:05:00,950
is a chance to start over.

68
00:05:25,310 --> 00:05:26,450
Rest well.

69
00:05:55,110 --> 00:06:00,390
[Your Third Series]

70
00:06:10,550 --> 00:06:14,480
♫Still feeling lonely?
Well, you've got me,♫

71
00:06:14,520 --> 00:06:18,960
♫Keeping you busy every day♫

72
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:23,620
♫I might not be the one you wanted,♫

73
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:28,380
♫But give it time, you'll love me anyway♫

74
00:06:28,830 --> 00:06:33,360
♫It's your heart, so it's your choice,♫

75
00:06:33,380 --> 00:06:37,820
♫I won't ever stand in your way♫

76
00:06:37,950 --> 00:06:42,210
♫But when they make you blue,♫

77
00:06:42,260 --> 00:06:45,970
♫Can you please let me take care of you?♫

78
00:06:46,940 --> 00:06:51,610
♫I'm here to love you as myself,
not as a surrogate♫

79
00:06:51,650 --> 00:06:55,400
♫Let me be your safe space
when you need a break♫

80
00:06:55,430 --> 00:07:00,420
♫Who cares
if I'm not your first or second?♫

81
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:04,970
♫At least being your third still counts♫

82
00:07:05,370 --> 00:07:09,920
♫I'm here to love you,
no matter who left you with heartache♫

83
00:07:09,970 --> 00:07:13,630
♫Just let me heal your heart,
lending you my aid♫

84
00:07:13,660 --> 00:07:18,770
♫Have faith and believe in love once more♫

85
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:20,780
♫'Cause good love is your Lucky Third♫

86
00:07:20,810 --> 00:07:24,010
♫Your Third, can it be me, love?♫

87
00:07:24,030 --> 00:07:26,980
[Your Third Series]

88
00:07:27,140 --> 00:07:27,750
Jam.

89
00:07:27,750 --> 00:07:28,430
Mr. Sarm?

90
00:07:32,670 --> 00:07:33,409
Little Jam...

91
00:07:33,890 --> 00:07:34,180
Little Jam!

92
00:07:34,180 --> 00:07:35,110
Sarm, Sarm.

93
00:07:35,110 --> 00:07:36,390
Calm down, calm down.

94
00:07:36,630 --> 00:07:37,110
Song,

95
00:07:37,340 --> 00:07:38,360
is Little Jam safe?

96
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:39,770
He is safe

97
00:07:40,250 --> 00:07:41,659
and has been treated.

98
00:07:43,480 --> 00:07:44,650
Rest easy, okay?

99
00:07:54,300 --> 00:07:56,360
He's in the waiting room right now.

100
00:07:57,560 --> 00:07:59,020
PiMai is trying to make him feel better.

101
00:08:01,610 --> 00:08:02,900
What time is it?

102
00:08:03,390 --> 00:08:04,760
It's almost 5 A.M.

103
00:08:06,340 --> 00:08:07,850
Am I hurt that badly?

104
00:08:08,560 --> 00:08:10,270
Why am I hospitalized?

105
00:08:11,170 --> 00:08:12,600
You're having another brain scan.

106
00:08:12,750 --> 00:08:13,370
Huh?

107
00:08:14,050 --> 00:08:15,360
It's to see if anything's wrong.

108
00:08:16,370 --> 00:08:17,510
Do I even have that thing?

109
00:08:19,710 --> 00:08:20,610
Knock, knock.

110
00:08:20,930 --> 00:08:22,300
Seems like you don't.

111
00:08:22,650 --> 00:08:24,690
That's why you were being so reckless.

112
00:08:25,050 --> 00:08:26,830
You almost lost your head, alright?

113
00:08:26,830 --> 00:08:27,900
Being my twin brother,

114
00:08:27,900 --> 00:08:29,270
you always scold me
or say nasty things to me.

115
00:08:29,270 --> 00:08:31,510
I'm a tiger with nine lives, alright?

116
00:08:31,670 --> 00:08:32,190
Right.

117
00:08:32,809 --> 00:08:34,090
I don't go down that easily.

118
00:08:34,090 --> 00:08:35,230
I hope that's true.

119
00:08:35,230 --> 00:08:36,659
Come on, you already know

120
00:08:36,659 --> 00:08:37,620
that I'm...

121
00:08:38,010 --> 00:08:39,150
tough.

122
00:08:41,960 --> 00:08:43,159
You people don't sleep or what?

123
00:08:43,480 --> 00:08:44,720
You already knew it, didn't you?

124
00:08:49,160 --> 00:08:50,020
I did.

125
00:08:55,160 --> 00:08:56,150
You mean I'm handsome, right?

126
00:08:56,150 --> 00:08:57,380
Not that, damn it!

127
00:08:59,010 --> 00:09:01,390
You knew that it was Thee
who sent men to hunt you down, right?

128
00:09:05,300 --> 00:09:05,960
Of course...

129
00:09:17,170 --> 00:09:18,180
Fine!

130
00:09:22,050 --> 00:09:22,950
I'll say it.

131
00:09:24,810 --> 00:09:26,530
I found out
when I got captured the second time.

132
00:09:26,860 --> 00:09:27,710
That night...

133
00:09:27,710 --> 00:09:29,330
I came back to my place
with Little Jam after dinner,

134
00:09:30,900 --> 00:09:32,130
and they were already waiting for me.

135
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:33,970
Then, I thought to myself,

136
00:09:33,970 --> 00:09:36,750
"How can I trace this back
to the person behind it?"

137
00:09:37,310 --> 00:09:38,990
So I pretended to let them capture me.

138
00:09:39,150 --> 00:09:40,650
They tried taking me to a deserted island,

139
00:09:40,910 --> 00:09:41,830
but I didn't let them.

140
00:09:41,830 --> 00:09:43,020
I fought back.

141
00:09:43,160 --> 00:09:44,110
I beat them up!

142
00:09:44,360 --> 00:09:45,050
Punched!

143
00:09:45,230 --> 00:09:46,040
Slammed!

144
00:09:46,140 --> 00:09:47,030
Hit!

145
00:09:47,150 --> 00:09:47,700
And punched!

146
00:09:47,700 --> 00:09:48,210
Mm!

147
00:09:48,480 --> 00:09:49,840
Then, they folded.

148
00:09:50,590 --> 00:09:51,950
They spit it out, telling me that

149
00:09:51,970 --> 00:09:52,900
it was Thee...

150
00:09:52,910 --> 00:09:53,960
who gave them the order.

151
00:09:55,160 --> 00:09:56,660
Curse you, Thee...

152
00:09:57,150 --> 00:09:58,500
If I hadn't been worried about Little Jam,

153
00:09:58,500 --> 00:09:59,660
I would've punched,

154
00:09:59,660 --> 00:10:00,490
hit,

155
00:10:00,490 --> 00:10:01,350
slammed,

156
00:10:01,350 --> 00:10:02,380
and punched them more!

157
00:10:02,590 --> 00:10:04,170
So luck was on their side, huh?

158
00:10:04,170 --> 00:10:05,130
Mm...

159
00:10:05,730 --> 00:10:06,700
So I quickly backtracked

160
00:10:06,910 --> 00:10:07,930
and jumped into the water.

161
00:10:08,330 --> 00:10:10,730
I swam, swam, swam.

162
00:10:10,970 --> 00:10:12,180
"Little Jam!

163
00:10:12,180 --> 00:10:13,390
Where are you, Little Jam?!"

164
00:10:13,550 --> 00:10:15,010
And I found him floating
in the middle of the sea.

165
00:10:15,010 --> 00:10:15,910
I asked myself...

166
00:10:15,910 --> 00:10:17,430
"Would he be okay?"

167
00:10:17,550 --> 00:10:19,160
So I swam him back to the shore.

168
00:10:19,160 --> 00:10:20,360
We ended up on Ko Samui.

169
00:10:21,390 --> 00:10:22,570
As for them,

170
00:10:22,920 --> 00:10:23,790
I pressured

171
00:10:24,260 --> 00:10:25,160
and squeezed them

172
00:10:25,310 --> 00:10:27,050
until they became key witnesses

173
00:10:27,050 --> 00:10:28,760
that would then seal Thee's fate.

174
00:10:29,140 --> 00:10:30,810
I simply have to call them,

175
00:10:31,770 --> 00:10:33,550
and they will make a grand reveal!

176
00:10:33,820 --> 00:10:34,730
It'll be glorious!

177
00:10:34,890 --> 00:10:35,960
And majestic!

178
00:10:36,620 --> 00:10:37,530
Oh...

179
00:10:37,530 --> 00:10:38,690
But it was too little, too late.

180
00:10:38,690 --> 00:10:39,560
Sheesh...

181
00:10:39,750 --> 00:10:41,300
I didn't get to be the star of the show.

182
00:10:41,850 --> 00:10:42,750
It's because of you, Sib.

183
00:10:42,750 --> 00:10:43,950
You sent Little Jam on a mission like that.

184
00:10:43,950 --> 00:10:44,730
And how did it go?

185
00:10:45,270 --> 00:10:46,190
Just look at this mess...

186
00:10:47,310 --> 00:10:49,160
I didn't know that you knew.

187
00:10:49,830 --> 00:10:51,560
That's why I sent Jam to look for evidence

188
00:10:52,090 --> 00:10:53,670
so that we can do it by the book.

189
00:10:56,360 --> 00:10:57,870
I didn't know that you knew.

190
00:10:59,850 --> 00:11:01,610
You should've told me what you were doing.

191
00:11:01,940 --> 00:11:02,750
What about Dad?

192
00:11:03,100 --> 00:11:04,290
Did he know anything?

193
00:11:05,060 --> 00:11:06,630
He told me that

194
00:11:06,630 --> 00:11:08,360
Uncle Mai was his friend

195
00:11:08,360 --> 00:11:10,180
back when they served
in the army in the South.

196
00:11:10,540 --> 00:11:12,570
Ever since Uncle Mai
found you at the beach,

197
00:11:12,710 --> 00:11:14,340
he has always been keeping Dad posted.

198
00:11:14,930 --> 00:11:16,130
Uncle Mai...

199
00:11:16,650 --> 00:11:18,450
The owner of the seafood restaurant?

200
00:11:19,620 --> 00:11:20,890
I never knew that.

201
00:11:20,890 --> 00:11:22,110
Oh, Uncle Mai.

202
00:11:22,540 --> 00:11:24,270
Whoa... You were pretty slick.

203
00:11:24,470 --> 00:11:26,730
And if I knew that Dad knew,

204
00:11:27,230 --> 00:11:27,830
I wouldn't have sent Jam

205
00:11:27,840 --> 00:11:29,390
to bring you back in the first place.

206
00:11:32,900 --> 00:11:35,230
None of us ever talk to one another, do we?

207
00:11:39,130 --> 00:11:40,050
And what about you?

208
00:11:40,050 --> 00:11:40,620
Hm?

209
00:11:40,620 --> 00:11:42,390
Did you know anything at all?

210
00:11:45,390 --> 00:11:46,550
I think I kind of did,

211
00:11:46,600 --> 00:11:47,680
but...

212
00:11:48,610 --> 00:11:49,860
I wasn't sure.

213
00:11:49,860 --> 00:11:51,130
Thought so.

214
00:11:51,950 --> 00:11:52,760
And...

215
00:11:53,070 --> 00:11:54,690
And what are we going to do about Thee?

216
00:11:58,720 --> 00:11:59,920
I'm taking this all the way.

217
00:12:00,390 --> 00:12:02,130
Bad guys don't get happy endings.

218
00:12:03,220 --> 00:12:04,570
The word "forgiveness"

219
00:12:05,060 --> 00:12:06,010
is not

220
00:12:06,030 --> 00:12:07,160
in my dictionary!

221
00:12:07,830 --> 00:12:08,930
Don't teach me what it means either.

222
00:12:09,560 --> 00:12:11,960
Thee, who I loved like a brother

223
00:12:12,480 --> 00:12:13,760
and trusted with everything,

224
00:12:14,020 --> 00:12:15,110
is now but a ghost!

225
00:12:19,010 --> 00:12:21,260
And I don't want to see
his face at Adisuan Farm again.

226
00:12:24,290 --> 00:12:25,830
You, my brother...

227
00:12:26,220 --> 00:12:27,330
love someone deeply when you do

228
00:12:27,330 --> 00:12:28,760
and despise the person when you hate them.

229
00:12:29,220 --> 00:12:30,650
You've always been like this
since you were a kid.

230
00:13:03,130 --> 00:13:04,190
Normally,

231
00:13:04,190 --> 00:13:06,490
I'd rush to my little boy.

232
00:13:06,490 --> 00:13:08,740
But this isn't normal.

233
00:13:10,250 --> 00:13:11,390
I'm still upset with him.

234
00:13:11,650 --> 00:13:12,830
I've asked him time and time again,

235
00:13:12,830 --> 00:13:14,590
yet he always hides the truth from me.

236
00:13:15,890 --> 00:13:17,550
I won't just be mad at him for a week,

237
00:13:17,940 --> 00:13:18,770
because this time...

238
00:13:18,780 --> 00:13:20,830
I'll be mad at him for months!
Just you wait!

239
00:13:21,140 --> 00:13:22,380
Why didn't you listen?!

240
00:13:22,940 --> 00:13:23,960
You're so stubborn!

241
00:13:26,620 --> 00:13:27,060
Mr. Sarm...

242
00:13:27,060 --> 00:13:28,020
Hold it right there!

243
00:13:34,470 --> 00:13:35,690
Not now.

244
00:13:57,290 --> 00:13:58,830
Your mission has ended.

245
00:13:59,540 --> 00:14:00,750
This evening...

246
00:14:00,750 --> 00:14:02,370
It's time for you to return to Bangkok.

247
00:14:07,490 --> 00:14:08,360
Understood.

248
00:15:41,500 --> 00:15:42,700
I'm here to return your glasses.

249
00:15:46,050 --> 00:15:47,110
Thank you.

250
00:15:54,780 --> 00:15:56,890
Your phone and your car key...

251
00:16:06,580 --> 00:16:07,380
Right.

252
00:16:08,110 --> 00:16:09,860
Your car will be brought over tomorrow.

253
00:16:10,940 --> 00:16:12,250
No need to drive it yourself.

254
00:16:12,930 --> 00:16:13,950
I'll have someone drive it to you.

255
00:16:14,610 --> 00:16:15,190
But...

256
00:16:15,190 --> 00:16:16,140
No buts.

257
00:16:24,100 --> 00:16:24,900
Hello.

258
00:16:27,020 --> 00:16:28,610
Escort Mr. Jam to his place.

259
00:16:31,790 --> 00:16:33,260
Drive as smoothly as you can.

260
00:16:35,580 --> 00:16:37,340
Do not go over 80 km/h.

261
00:16:39,820 --> 00:16:41,960
Report back to me
once you reach the destination.

262
00:16:45,060 --> 00:16:47,230
Do not forget to warn him
to wear a seat belt

263
00:16:48,620 --> 00:16:49,830
because he's just that stubborn.

264
00:16:51,480 --> 00:16:52,390
He refuses to listen.

265
00:16:59,780 --> 00:17:00,870
And don't eat

266
00:17:02,230 --> 00:17:03,560
instant noodles too often.

267
00:17:05,069 --> 00:17:07,160
Eat some actual food.

268
00:17:10,140 --> 00:17:11,050
Mm.

269
00:17:12,490 --> 00:17:14,359
Don't overwork yourself.

270
00:17:15,690 --> 00:17:17,410
Can't keep working
round the clock like this.

271
00:17:17,849 --> 00:17:18,690
Get some rest.

272
00:17:21,450 --> 00:17:22,569
Wherever you go,

273
00:17:22,569 --> 00:17:24,410
keep your eyes peeled.

274
00:17:26,869 --> 00:17:27,849
I know that you've got this,

275
00:17:29,590 --> 00:17:30,910
but nobody's there to take care of you

276
00:17:32,590 --> 00:17:33,910
when you're living there alone.

277
00:17:43,120 --> 00:17:44,510
As for boiled crabs...

278
00:17:45,560 --> 00:17:47,220
the ones from here are the best.

279
00:17:55,500 --> 00:17:57,370
Do not forget
to take care of yourself, too.

280
00:18:22,910 --> 00:18:26,630
I should be happy
because I'm done with Mr. Sarm.

281
00:18:28,110 --> 00:18:29,960
But why is it the opposite?

282
00:18:57,390 --> 00:18:59,250
I haven't gotten to ask him
to be my boyfriend

283
00:18:59,250 --> 00:19:02,080
or wrap myself up as his present.

284
00:19:02,510 --> 00:19:03,390
Why?

285
00:19:03,560 --> 00:19:04,760
Just why?

286
00:19:22,230 --> 00:19:23,960
Look...

287
00:19:25,710 --> 00:19:27,940
This is Mr. Croc,
my beloved crocodile plush.

288
00:19:32,030 --> 00:19:33,520
I love him so much.

289
00:19:33,540 --> 00:19:35,800
Can I bring Mr. Croc to Pak Chong with me?

290
00:19:43,630 --> 00:19:45,180
Why did your boss send you here?

291
00:19:47,470 --> 00:19:49,770
To learn the ins and outs of this farm.

292
00:19:51,730 --> 00:19:53,190
Are you sure?

293
00:19:55,010 --> 00:19:56,360
Don't hide anything from me.

294
00:20:02,770 --> 00:20:03,560
Mm.

295
00:20:05,750 --> 00:20:06,860
Okay.

296
00:20:06,860 --> 00:20:08,110
I believe you.

297
00:20:24,420 --> 00:20:26,360
Are you sure you actually lost?

298
00:20:30,850 --> 00:20:31,770
Mm.

299
00:20:33,690 --> 00:20:35,070
Are you certain

300
00:20:35,510 --> 00:20:37,160
that you're not plotting anything?

301
00:20:41,550 --> 00:20:43,410
I am doing nothing.

302
00:20:45,810 --> 00:20:47,390
I'll give you one more chance.

303
00:20:47,650 --> 00:20:48,830
Spit it out.

304
00:20:51,820 --> 00:20:53,660
I said I wasn't plotting anything.

305
00:20:56,980 --> 00:20:57,810
Okay.

306
00:20:57,950 --> 00:20:59,630
But if I catch you lying,

307
00:21:00,150 --> 00:21:01,410
even if it's you,

308
00:21:01,780 --> 00:21:03,560
I won't let it slide.

309
00:21:05,380 --> 00:21:06,590
Why?

310
00:21:09,210 --> 00:21:11,380
If I really am hiding something from you...

311
00:21:13,710 --> 00:21:15,020
That was just a hypothetical situation

312
00:21:15,690 --> 00:21:16,990
and nothing else.

313
00:21:17,820 --> 00:21:19,160
I'd be furious.

314
00:21:19,160 --> 00:21:20,650
I'd be mad at you
for a whole week.

315
00:21:29,830 --> 00:21:33,150
You can be mad at me for a week if you want,

316
00:21:34,970 --> 00:21:37,660
but you have to forgive me after that, okay?

317
00:21:49,410 --> 00:21:50,390
Look at you...

318
00:21:52,900 --> 00:21:53,920
What a mess.

319
00:22:01,690 --> 00:22:03,210
This man...

320
00:22:03,900 --> 00:22:05,650
He's worn out...

321
00:22:10,540 --> 00:22:11,430
Not that big of a deal.

322
00:22:11,430 --> 00:22:12,410
Huh?

323
00:22:12,940 --> 00:22:14,360
"Not that big of a deal?"

324
00:22:14,660 --> 00:22:16,380
You did this to yourself, Sarm.

325
00:22:16,760 --> 00:22:17,700
I think

326
00:22:19,330 --> 00:22:21,300
"not that big of a deal
is different for everyone."

327
00:22:21,890 --> 00:22:23,330
Someone I trusted...

328
00:22:23,330 --> 00:22:24,950
sent his men to get rid of me.

329
00:22:26,360 --> 00:22:27,560
Ow...

330
00:22:29,430 --> 00:22:31,430
I think I've developed

331
00:22:31,430 --> 00:22:32,740
trust issues.

332
00:22:36,730 --> 00:22:38,140
I can no longer trust anyone.

333
00:22:42,670 --> 00:22:43,660
Hey...

334
00:22:43,970 --> 00:22:45,190
I'm sorry.

335
00:22:45,190 --> 00:22:46,110
I...

336
00:22:47,850 --> 00:22:49,790
I forgot about that.

337
00:22:51,300 --> 00:22:52,380
Listen...

338
00:22:54,210 --> 00:22:55,850
And out of nowhere,

339
00:22:57,740 --> 00:22:58,760
Little Jam...

340
00:22:59,510 --> 00:23:00,850
was sent here.

341
00:23:03,180 --> 00:23:04,030
I always

342
00:23:04,490 --> 00:23:05,960
had my suspicions about him.

343
00:23:06,730 --> 00:23:07,780
I asked

344
00:23:07,780 --> 00:23:08,970
what his goal was,

345
00:23:09,210 --> 00:23:10,890
but I never got an answer!

346
00:23:10,890 --> 00:23:13,160
He just kept dodging my questions...

347
00:23:14,700 --> 00:23:16,420
I asked him so many times, too.

348
00:23:17,670 --> 00:23:19,890
He had no intention
of hiding it from you, Sarm.

349
00:23:20,190 --> 00:23:20,990
It's Sib.

350
00:23:21,260 --> 00:23:23,370
He was following our big brother's order.

351
00:23:24,220 --> 00:23:24,820
Listen.

352
00:23:24,990 --> 00:23:25,850
I'm

353
00:23:26,550 --> 00:23:28,150
upset at both of them.

354
00:23:30,350 --> 00:23:32,070
But I'm mad at them for different reasons.

355
00:23:34,550 --> 00:23:35,750
Look at this plush.

356
00:23:36,810 --> 00:23:37,860
Just look at it.

357
00:23:39,940 --> 00:23:41,210
It's staring at me like this.

358
00:23:41,210 --> 00:23:42,190
I'm in this state,

359
00:23:42,190 --> 00:23:43,160
and yet you dare stare at me?

360
00:23:43,160 --> 00:23:45,010
You dare keep staring at me?

361
00:23:45,010 --> 00:23:45,940
What?!

362
00:23:45,940 --> 00:23:47,030
Got beef with me?!

363
00:23:47,330 --> 00:23:48,710
You're not going to feel sorry

364
00:23:48,710 --> 00:23:50,020
or show any remorse at all?

365
00:23:50,020 --> 00:23:51,150
What is it, huh?!

366
00:23:51,740 --> 00:23:52,680
How do you want to settle this?!

367
00:23:55,850 --> 00:23:56,610
What was that for?

368
00:23:58,510 --> 00:23:59,360
Go away.

369
00:24:00,570 --> 00:24:02,100
But with Little Jam, you see...

370
00:24:02,100 --> 00:24:02,360
Mm.

371
00:24:02,360 --> 00:24:03,560
I...

372
00:24:04,050 --> 00:24:05,680
I didn't quit trying.

373
00:24:07,200 --> 00:24:09,260
My feelings toward him haven't changed.

374
00:24:11,570 --> 00:24:12,890
I'm just confused.

375
00:24:18,570 --> 00:24:19,350
But...

376
00:24:20,160 --> 00:24:21,110
Why did he...

377
00:24:21,110 --> 00:24:23,060
He didn't even try to make it up to me?

378
00:24:26,220 --> 00:24:27,950
You want Jam to make it up to you?

379
00:24:30,700 --> 00:24:32,100
But you always looked...

380
00:24:32,100 --> 00:24:33,930
extremely unfriendly toward him.

381
00:24:34,610 --> 00:24:35,380
Gosh...

382
00:24:35,380 --> 00:24:36,870
Given the situation,

383
00:24:37,520 --> 00:24:39,080
how am I supposed to keep smiling?

384
00:24:39,410 --> 00:24:40,760
I can't.

385
00:24:46,760 --> 00:24:47,960
I simply can't.

386
00:24:48,780 --> 00:24:50,060
And what are you feeling exactly?

387
00:24:50,590 --> 00:24:51,380
Are you angry?

388
00:24:51,850 --> 00:24:52,760
Furious?

389
00:24:53,010 --> 00:24:53,960
Sad?

390
00:24:55,160 --> 00:24:56,670
Or upset?

391
00:25:07,140 --> 00:25:08,060
All of the above.

392
00:25:08,060 --> 00:25:08,710
Mm.

393
00:25:08,980 --> 00:25:09,560
I...

394
00:25:09,630 --> 00:25:10,630
I don't know.

395
00:25:10,940 --> 00:25:12,380
I'm feeling all of them at once.

396
00:25:12,770 --> 00:25:14,500
If I were a bowl of spicy salad,

397
00:25:14,500 --> 00:25:16,430
I'd be one with everything in it.

398
00:25:16,830 --> 00:25:18,370
Even if I got mad at him,

399
00:25:19,950 --> 00:25:21,350
he wouldn't make it up to me.

400
00:25:24,080 --> 00:25:25,160
I'm so upset...

401
00:25:35,170 --> 00:25:36,650
You love Jam, don't you?

402
00:25:36,980 --> 00:25:38,360
Of course, I do.

403
00:25:39,300 --> 00:25:40,490
I love Little Jam.

404
00:25:41,490 --> 00:25:42,970
I love him so much.

405
00:25:43,620 --> 00:25:45,150
I love him more than anyone.

406
00:25:46,890 --> 00:25:47,770
Hey.

407
00:25:47,770 --> 00:25:48,980
I, Traiphop,

408
00:25:49,390 --> 00:25:50,940
love Jiranat

409
00:25:52,460 --> 00:25:53,770
forever.

410
00:25:54,650 --> 00:25:55,900
If you love him,

411
00:25:56,830 --> 00:25:58,370
why did you let your emotions

412
00:25:58,900 --> 00:26:00,220
take over?

413
00:26:03,560 --> 00:26:04,760
What should I do, then?

414
00:26:05,730 --> 00:26:06,980
If I were you,

415
00:26:08,150 --> 00:26:10,410
I wouldn't wait around any longer.

416
00:26:11,130 --> 00:26:12,710
We're all grownups now.

417
00:26:13,430 --> 00:26:15,090
Don't complicate things.

418
00:26:16,390 --> 00:26:17,960
If you miss him,

419
00:26:18,380 --> 00:26:19,420
just say it.

420
00:26:19,980 --> 00:26:21,410
If you want to hear his voice,

421
00:26:22,630 --> 00:26:24,220
just call him.

422
00:26:25,770 --> 00:26:26,780
Or...

423
00:26:27,150 --> 00:26:28,550
If you want to see him,

424
00:26:29,270 --> 00:26:30,780
just go see him.

425
00:26:31,270 --> 00:26:32,540
It's as simple as that.

426
00:26:38,710 --> 00:26:39,560
Mm...

427
00:26:40,270 --> 00:26:41,380
Thank you very much, Song.

428
00:26:43,160 --> 00:26:44,750
It's like you've experienced it before.

429
00:26:46,410 --> 00:26:47,670
Who did that to you?

430
00:26:47,670 --> 00:26:48,540
It's okay.

431
00:26:48,540 --> 00:26:49,660
You've still got me.

432
00:26:49,660 --> 00:26:50,690
Listen, I'm right here.

433
00:26:50,690 --> 00:26:51,230
I'm here...

434
00:26:51,230 --> 00:26:51,970
- Let me kiss you.
- It's okay...

435
00:26:51,970 --> 00:26:53,390
- I'm good...
- Come here.

436
00:26:53,730 --> 00:26:54,220
Stupid Sarm.

437
00:26:54,220 --> 00:26:56,360
You should feel sorry about yourself first.

438
00:26:58,580 --> 00:26:59,960
Take a look at yourself.

439
00:27:02,480 --> 00:27:03,570
You're like a wet dog.

440
00:27:09,690 --> 00:27:11,750
Aunt Nim made you
five-spice stew in a tiffin box.

441
00:27:11,750 --> 00:27:12,660
Don't forget to eat the stew.

442
00:27:12,660 --> 00:27:13,550
Right.

443
00:27:13,820 --> 00:27:14,360
You can go now.

444
00:27:14,360 --> 00:27:15,270
See you.

445
00:27:17,270 --> 00:27:18,420
What is it now?

446
00:27:20,310 --> 00:27:20,810
What's wrong?

447
00:27:20,810 --> 00:27:22,530
You didn't tell me sweet dreams.

448
00:27:22,630 --> 00:27:23,390
"Sweet dreams"?

449
00:27:23,620 --> 00:27:24,640
Am I Jam or what?

450
00:27:25,330 --> 00:27:26,360
Don't mention that name.

451
00:27:26,360 --> 00:27:28,300
There, there, there.

452
00:27:28,300 --> 00:27:29,250
It's okay. It's okay.

453
00:27:29,250 --> 00:27:29,960
Okay, well, then...

454
00:27:29,960 --> 00:27:31,160
Sweet dreams.

455
00:27:31,160 --> 00:27:32,360
Good night, good night.

456
00:27:32,360 --> 00:27:33,270
Okay...

457
00:27:33,270 --> 00:27:33,910
Good night.

458
00:27:34,530 --> 00:27:35,430
Bye-bye.

459
00:27:35,960 --> 00:27:37,050
I'm leaving now, okay?

460
00:27:39,410 --> 00:27:40,410
See you, alright?

461
00:27:44,360 --> 00:27:45,560
Again?

462
00:27:45,560 --> 00:27:47,030
You've stopped kissing me on the head.

463
00:27:47,030 --> 00:27:47,960
A kiss on my head! Come on!

464
00:27:47,960 --> 00:27:48,580
A kiss on your head?

465
00:27:49,900 --> 00:27:51,350
You used to do it every night.

466
00:27:51,350 --> 00:27:51,970
Fine, come here.

467
00:27:51,970 --> 00:27:52,760
Here comes a kiss on the head.

468
00:27:52,760 --> 00:27:55,760
Here comes your kiss on the head...

469
00:27:58,060 --> 00:27:58,760
Better now?

470
00:27:58,760 --> 00:28:00,130
Yes, you can leave now...

471
00:28:00,130 --> 00:28:01,160
- Better?
- Mm.

472
00:28:03,220 --> 00:28:04,140
Bye-bye.

473
00:28:04,140 --> 00:28:06,510
You've been extremely weird
since you were a kid.

474
00:28:06,660 --> 00:28:07,870
Don't forget that

475
00:28:07,870 --> 00:28:10,040
we're twins.

476
00:28:10,590 --> 00:28:11,470
If I'm weird,

477
00:28:11,470 --> 00:28:12,940
then so are you.

478
00:28:14,900 --> 00:28:15,890
Oh, you.

479
00:28:16,200 --> 00:28:17,440
You, of all people...

480
00:28:17,960 --> 00:28:18,960
are such a pain.

481
00:28:19,370 --> 00:28:20,230
Damn you, Sarm!

482
00:28:20,230 --> 00:28:20,650
Bye.

483
00:28:20,650 --> 00:28:21,330
I'm leaving for real now.

484
00:28:21,330 --> 00:28:22,290
Right.

485
00:28:27,430 --> 00:28:29,960
I miss you, Little Jam!

486
00:28:31,160 --> 00:28:32,140
Little Jam...

487
00:28:34,450 --> 00:28:35,980
I miss you...

488
00:28:36,420 --> 00:28:37,670
Little Jam.

489
00:28:38,150 --> 00:28:39,390
Oh, Little Jam...

490
00:28:39,670 --> 00:28:40,760
Little Jam...

491
00:28:41,070 --> 00:28:43,160
Little Jam, I miss you.

492
00:28:43,160 --> 00:28:44,480
Little Jam...

493
00:28:45,560 --> 00:28:46,760
Little Jam!

494
00:28:48,510 --> 00:28:49,160
Whoa.

495
00:29:03,310 --> 00:29:05,360
This house is full of scary animals.

496
00:29:16,900 --> 00:29:18,390
Little Jam!

497
00:29:47,680 --> 00:29:49,140
Your house is very lovely, you know?

498
00:29:51,380 --> 00:29:54,700
♫I came this far just to meet you♫

499
00:29:54,700 --> 00:30:01,510
♫There's so much you've been through♫

500
00:30:01,510 --> 00:30:04,900
♫But that doesn't matter♫

501
00:30:04,900 --> 00:30:08,210
♫Time stood still when I met you♫

502
00:30:08,210 --> 00:30:11,620
♫The way you gazed at me too♫

503
00:30:13,160 --> 00:30:14,590
Are you hitting on me?

504
00:30:14,790 --> 00:30:16,390
Yes, just now realizing that?

505
00:30:35,510 --> 00:30:38,780
♫I came this far just to meet you♫

506
00:30:38,780 --> 00:30:45,560
♫There's so much you've been through♫

507
00:30:45,560 --> 00:30:49,020
♫But that doesn't matter♫

508
00:30:49,020 --> 00:30:52,380
♫Mend your heart, make it better♫

509
00:30:52,380 --> 00:30:55,710
♫Whatever it is, you don't need to fear,♫

510
00:30:55,710 --> 00:31:02,500
♫For I'll be right here by your side like always♫

511
00:31:02,500 --> 00:31:08,770
♫It seems like something's moving♫

512
00:31:08,770 --> 00:31:15,330
♫What's in my heart isn't too much, but I only♫

513
00:31:16,210 --> 00:31:17,700
You silly...

514
00:31:18,390 --> 00:31:21,090
I already miss you just watching this.

515
00:31:21,700 --> 00:31:23,270
Everything looks perfectly normal.

516
00:31:29,400 --> 00:31:30,210
Little Jam!

517
00:31:30,230 --> 00:31:30,700
Whoa, Mr. Sarm?!

518
00:31:30,700 --> 00:31:31,850
- Little Jam!
- How did you get here?

519
00:31:32,910 --> 00:31:33,390
Little Jam...

520
00:31:33,390 --> 00:31:34,760
Hey...

521
00:31:36,860 --> 00:31:38,900
No matter what I do,

522
00:31:40,020 --> 00:31:41,960
where I go,

523
00:31:42,160 --> 00:31:43,810
or where I look,

524
00:31:45,380 --> 00:31:47,750
I always see his face.

525
00:32:03,810 --> 00:32:05,410
Juju.

526
00:32:06,310 --> 00:32:08,130
What should I do?

527
00:32:10,760 --> 00:32:13,620
I cannot stop thinking about Mr. Sarm.

528
00:32:55,570 --> 00:32:57,130
How are you guys doing?

529
00:33:00,710 --> 00:33:01,960
Why did you ask that question?

530
00:33:02,590 --> 00:33:03,910
So what if I'm doing well?

531
00:33:04,090 --> 00:33:05,500
And what if I'm not?

532
00:33:05,830 --> 00:33:07,780
Are you going to cut my salary?

533
00:33:09,040 --> 00:33:10,480
I'd like to make it clear that

534
00:33:10,500 --> 00:33:12,720
I will not let you cut my salary.

535
00:33:13,780 --> 00:33:15,560
The only thing that can be cut

536
00:33:16,180 --> 00:33:18,330
is my love for you!

537
00:33:19,160 --> 00:33:20,990
You can't just be hangry and take it on me.

538
00:33:23,170 --> 00:33:23,890
Anything else you want?

539
00:33:23,910 --> 00:33:24,530
It's on me.

540
00:33:24,850 --> 00:33:26,150
No need to treat me to anything, Sarm.

541
00:33:26,810 --> 00:33:27,810
Why is that?

542
00:33:28,000 --> 00:33:29,720
It's because I can treat myself.

543
00:33:31,500 --> 00:33:32,870
Right...fantastic.

544
00:33:35,650 --> 00:33:37,160
Do you love Jam, Sarm?

545
00:33:39,560 --> 00:33:40,210
Yes,

546
00:33:40,740 --> 00:33:41,640
I love Jam.

547
00:33:46,340 --> 00:33:47,670
I knew it...

548
00:33:49,540 --> 00:33:51,110
The night at the New Year party,

549
00:33:51,730 --> 00:33:53,960
when you two kissed,

550
00:33:55,450 --> 00:33:57,410
I accidentally saw it.

551
00:34:00,950 --> 00:34:01,620
Mm...

552
00:34:01,950 --> 00:34:03,190
It has been clear since then.

553
00:34:04,070 --> 00:34:05,950
Tell Jam to shower you with love

554
00:34:07,530 --> 00:34:09,790
and love you
as much as I've been hurt!

555
00:34:15,409 --> 00:34:16,500
Are you okay?

556
00:34:17,409 --> 00:34:18,370
It doesn't matter anymore.

557
00:34:18,980 --> 00:34:20,960
It's okay if our love got cut short.

558
00:34:20,980 --> 00:34:23,370
At least my priority was
making good memories together,

559
00:34:23,570 --> 00:34:24,889
even if you didn't choose me.

560
00:34:26,620 --> 00:34:28,190
I'll have to take my leave now.

561
00:34:31,830 --> 00:34:33,560
Then I'll go with him.

562
00:34:33,699 --> 00:34:34,760
Wait, Mr. Wasin.

563
00:34:35,210 --> 00:34:36,760
You invited me here.

564
00:34:36,860 --> 00:34:37,790
And...

565
00:34:39,020 --> 00:34:41,110
Since when am I out of the loop?

566
00:34:42,090 --> 00:34:43,159
Uh...

567
00:34:43,159 --> 00:34:45,980
Back at the New Year party,

568
00:34:46,870 --> 00:34:48,560
Lantao dressed as a medium

569
00:34:48,650 --> 00:34:50,010
to exorcise ghosts.

570
00:34:50,550 --> 00:34:52,090
